 rounding, giving point 217.4 + 10.0 + 6.0 = 233.4 thousand. Interval method uses the values themselves for this flow proxy: sigma = 9.6 thousand across the three five-week analogs, so 1.28*sigma = 12.3 thousand. I widen to a judgmental 40.0 thousand half-width, beyond 1.75x, because the fetched annual DI workload anchors are not the exact monthly DDS Field I target series and the conditional policy mechanism could shift filings around April 2027; final implied bounds are 233.4 +/- 40.0 = 193.4 to 273.4 thousand.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Counter-considerations: upside risk is a larger Medicaid work-requirement response, outreach by advocates, or SSA/DDS intake catch-up that would land above the interval if April 2027 exceeds 273.4 thousand. Downside risk under the stated condition is weak take-up, limited awareness of disability pathways, administrative friction, or filings shifted outside April; the outcome would land below the interval if receipts are under 193.4 thousand. An outside the interval high print would most likely require a broad policy-driven filing surge rather than normal trend.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Review disposition: accepted the critiques to clarify that annual DI workload values are a proxy rather than monthly Field I history, reduce the Medicaid policy adjustment from +12.0 to +6.0 thousand, widen and label the interval as judgmental, remove federal delay as a conditional downside tail, and clarify that 2027-05-30 is the SSA update-rule availability deadline while first replacement file remains the resolver.\"},{\"kind\":\"forecast\",\"point\":233.4,\"ciLow\":193.4,\"ciHigh\":273.4}]}\n./records/thesis-analyst/2026-07-08/2026-07-08t21-21-56z-ssa-dds-initial-disability-receipts-2027-04/normalized_cells.json:17:    \"dataPointId\": \"ssa.dds.initial_disability_receipts.2027-04.first_print\",\n./records/thesis-analyst/2026-07-08/2026-07-08t21-21-56z-ssa-dds-initial-disability-receipts-2027-04/revision_prompt.md:11:- series: ssa.