t Friday of the month, the Date field maps to SSA time periods, and the dataset is updated with a new time period within 30 days of the close of the prior time period; April 2027's last Friday is 2027-04-30, so the official within-30-days by-date is 2027-05-30.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened Annual Statistical Supplement 2025 Agency Workloads, Table 2.F5 and 2.F6, for latest official claim-volume anchor.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched fiscal year 2024 claims workloads: Disability Insurance claims received total 2,260.6 thousand, worker 2,145.9 thousand, family members and survivors 114.7 thousand; SSI claims received total 1,683.2 thousand, aged 214.1 thousand, blind or disabled 1,469.1 thousand.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened Annual Statistical Supplement 2024 Claims Workloads, Table 2.F5 and 2.F6, for prior-year official anchor.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched fiscal year 2023 claims workloads: Disability Insurance claims received total 2,111.9 thousand, worker 2,000.7 thousand, family members and survivors 111.2 thousand; SSI blind or disabled claims received 1,395.6 thousand.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened Annual Statistical Supplement 2023 Claims Workloads, Table 2.F5 and 2.F6, for older official anchor.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched fiscal year 2022 claims workloads: Disability Insurance claims received total 2,071.7 thousand, worker 1,960.0 thousand, family members and survivors 111.7 thousand; SSI blind or disabled claims received 1,271.9 thousand.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Base rate/reference class: the best fetched official-source class available in this run is recent SSA disability-related claims workload volume. DI total claims received rose from 2,071.7 thousand in FY2022 to 2,111.9 thousand in FY2023 and 2,260.6 thousand in FY2024, equal to simple monthly equivalents of 172.6, 176.0, and 188.4 thousand. The DDS Field I resolver is a monthly flow, so I anchor on a five-week April month rather than a calendar-month stock.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Level, momentum, one-off, and policy mechanism: level starts from the FY2024 monthly-equivalent DI claims volume because the raw SSA-SA-MOWL.csv was identified as the final resolver but was not readable as tabular rows through the draft environment; this makes the annual DI workload prior a downgraded proxy rather than the target-series monthly history. Momentum is upward across FY2022-FY2024; the one-off calendar effect is that April 2027 normally spans five SSA weekly closes; the conditional Medicaid community-engagement mechanism adds a judgmental, scenario-weighted filing-pressure adjustment, but I reduce it because the draft did not fetch a direct eligibility-channeling analog.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"math\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Prior/update/interval: persistence prior = FY2024 DI claims received monthly equivalent 2,260.6/12 = 188.4 thousand; historical sample = fetched FY2022-FY2024 DI monthly equivalents converted to five-week SSA-month analogs using 5/(52/12)=1.1538, giving 199.2, 203.1, and 217.4 thousand; adjustment components = +10.0 thousand for partial continuation of the FY2022-FY2024 upward trend into 2027, +6.0 thousand for the conditional Medicaid community-engagement deadline pull-forward/channeling mechanism, and +0.0 for rounding, giving point 217.4 + 10.0 + 6.0 = 233.4 thousand. Interval method uses the values themselves for this flow proxy: sigma = 9.6 thousand across the three five-week analogs, so 1.28*sigma = 12.3 thousand. I widen to a judgmental 40.0 thousand half-width, beyond 1.75x, because the fetched annual DI workload anchors are not the exact monthly DDS Field I target series and the conditional policy mechanism could shift filings around April 2027; final implied bounds are 233.4 +/- 40.0 = 193.4 to 273.4 thousand.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Counter-considerations: upside risk is a larger Medicaid work-requirement response, outreach by advocates, or SSA/DDS intake catch-up that would land above the interval if April 2027 exceeds 273.4 thousand. Downside risk under the stated condition is weak take-up, limited awareness of disability pathways, administrative friction, or filings shifted outside April; the outcome would land below the interval if receipts are under 193.4 thousand. An outside the interval high print would most likely require a broad policy-driven filing surge rather than normal trend.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Review disposition: accepted the critiques to clarify that annual DI workload values are a proxy rather than monthly Field I history, reduce the Medicaid policy adjustment from +12.0 to +6.0 thousand, widen and label the interval as judgmental, remove federal delay as a conditional downside tail, and clarify that 2027-05-30 is the SSA update-rule availability deadline while first replacement file remains the resolver.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"forecast\\\",\\\"point\\\":233.4,\\\"ciLow\\\":193.4,\\\"ciHigh\\\":273.4}]}\"}}\n./records/thesis-analyst/2026-07-08/2026-07-08t21-21-56z-ssa-dds-initial-disability-receipts-2027-04/draft_stdout.txt:1:{\"slug\":\"ssdi-initial-applications-april-2027-work-req-deadline-holds\",\"country\":\"US\",\"type\":\"conditional\",\"title\":\"SSDI initial applications, Apr 2027\",\"question\":\"Social Security Administration State Agency Monthly Workload Data, Field I Receipts (All Initial), SSA month 2027-04, not seasonally adjusted, first print, in thousands, conditional on the 2025 reconciliation law's Medicaid community-engagement compliance deadline taking effect on its statutory schedule with no federal statutory or regulatory delay announced by 2027-03-31\",\"unit\":\"thousands\",\"pointEstimate\":239.4,\"ciLow\":209.4,\"ciHigh\":269.4,\"confidence\":0.8,\"resolutionDate\":\"202