,{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Framing and exact resolver: this forecast targets SSA State Agency Monthly Workload Data monthly Field I, Receipts (All Initial), for SSA month 2027-04. The variant is not seasonally adjusted DDS/state-agency initial claims, not OASDI beneficiary stocks, not SSI Monthly Statistics, and not final revised annual claims workloads.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened SSA State Agency Monthly Workload Data documentation and data dictionary.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched official dataset facts: monthly data start in October 2000; the expanded current file has 71 data elements; Field I is Receipts (All Initial); Fields I-M cover All Initial Claims; data are one row per State Code and Date; no summary row is provided; File Version currently has value 2.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened SSA State Agency Monthly Workload Data timing and update-policy documentation.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched timing evidence: SSA counts monthly work in weekly increments, an SSA month normally ends on the last Friday of the month, the Date field maps to SSA time periods, and the dataset is updated with a new time period within 30 days of the close of the prior time period; April 2027's last Friday is 2027-04-30, so the official within-30-days by-date is 2027-05-30.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened Annual Statistical Supplement 2025 Agency Workloads, Table 2.F5 and 2.F6, for latest official claim-volume anchor.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched fiscal year 2024 claims workloads: Disability Insurance claims received total 2,260.6 thousand, worker 2,145.9 thousand, family members and survivors 114.7 thousand; SSI claims received total 1,683.2 thousand, aged 214.1 thousand, blind or disabled 1,469.1 thousand.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened Annual Statistical Supplement 2024 Claims Workloads, Table 2.F5 and 2.F6, for prior-year official anchor.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched fiscal year 2023 claims workloads: Disability Insurance claims received total 2,111.9 thousand, worker 2,000.7 thousand, family members and survivors 111.2 thousand; SSI blind or disabled claims received 1,395.6 thousand.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened Annual Statistical Supplement 2023 Claims Workloads, Table 2.F5 and 2.F6, for older official anchor.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched fiscal year 2022 claims workloads: Disability Insurance claims received total 2,071.7 thousand, worker 1,960.0 thousand, family members and survivors 111.7 thousand; SSI blind or disabled claims received 1,271.9 thousand.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Base rate/reference class: the best fetched official-source class available in this run is recent SSA disability-related claims workload volume. DI total claims received rose from 2,071.7 thousand in FY2022 to 2,111.9 thousand in FY2023 and 2,260.6 thousand in FY2024, equal to simple monthly equivalents of 172.6, 176.0, and 188.4 thousand. The DDS Field I resolver is a monthly flow, so I anchor on a five-week April month rather than a calendar-month stock.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Level, momentum, one-off, and policy mechanism: level starts from the FY2024 monthly-equivalent DI claims volume because the raw SSA-SA-MOWL.csv was identified as the final resolver but not readable as tabular rows through this environment; momentum is upward across FY2022-FY2024; the one-off calendar effect is that April 2027 normally spans five SSA weekly closes; the conditional Medicaid community-engagement mechanism adds some near-term disability-claim filing pressure as affected adults seek disability status or disability-benefit eligibility routes, but the effect should be modest relative to national claims volume.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"math\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Prior/update/interval: persistence prior = FY2024 DI claims received monthly equivalent 2,260.6/12 = 188.4 thousand; historical sample = fetched FY2022-FY2024 DI monthly equivalents converted to five-week SSA-month analogs using 5/(52/12)=1.1538, giving 199.2, 203.1, and 217.4 thousand; adjustment components = +10.0 thousand for partial continuation of the FY2022-FY2024 upward trend into 2027, +12.0 thousand for the conditional Medicaid community-engagement deadline pull-forward/channeling mechanism, and +0.0 for rounding, giving point 217.4 + 10.0 + 12.0 = 239.4 thousand. Interval method uses the values themselves for this flow series: sigma = 9.6 thousand across the three five-week analogs, so 1.28*sigma = 12.3 thousand. I widen to a 30.0 thousand half-width because the fetched annual DI workload anchors are an imperfect proxy for the exact monthly DDS Field I all-initial resolver and because the conditional policy mechanism could concentrate applications around the deadline; final implied bounds are 239.4 +/- 30.0 = 209.4 to 269.4 thousand.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Counter-considerations: upside risk is a larger Medicaid work-requirement response, outreach by advocates, or SSA/DDS intake catch-up that would land above the interval if April 2027 exceeds 269.4 thousand. Downside risk is a federal delay announced by 2027-03-31, weak disability-application response, or administrative bottlenecks shifting filings after April; under the stated condition, the outcome would land below the interval if receipts are under 209.4 thousand. An outside the interval high print would most likely require a broad policy-driven filing surge rather than normal trend.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"forecast\\\",\\\"point\\\":239.4,\\\"ciLow\\\":209.4,\\\"ciHigh\\\":269.4}]}\\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-07-08/2026-07-08t21-21-56z-ssa-dds-initial-disability-receipts-2027-04/prompt.md:11:- series: ssa.dds.